# <APP>-ARCH-001 — <Application> architecture overview

## Scope, source versions, and constraints

Link the approved spec/design versions, feasibility evidence, platform requirements, and known open decisions.

## System context and trust boundaries

Describe users, operators, systems, data boundaries, identities/permissions, and what is explicitly outside the system.

## Component/data ownership and flows

Describe high-level components, source of truth, sensitive data, state transitions, retention/deletion, provenance, and key interfaces. Link detailed contracts rather than duplicating them.

## External integrations and failure behavior

For every integration, state status (proposed/selected/verified), owner, auth boundary, data sent/received, timeouts/retries/idempotency, rate/cost limits, outage/partial/unknown behavior, and fallback.

## Security, privacy, accessibility, reliability, and operations

Link threat assessment, controls, recovery, observability, platform audit needs, deployment and support ownership. Keep unverified controls open.

## Alternatives and architecture decisions

Link ADRs and state any remaining decisions that block implementation.

## Implementation readiness

Link tasks with requirement IDs, dependencies, acceptance criteria, verification plan, and gate status. Do not treat diagrams as proof that contracts are implemented.
